{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like","id":968202,"title":"What would an 'endgame' book look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T15:48:00-07:00","id":968202,"title":"What would an 'endgame' book look like?","content":"Werewolf has one of the smaller lines in 1e, but covered the majority of interesting topics that needed to be hit and then some. While 2e has some work to do in detailing the new focuses with the edition shift (The Pack was a great example of this), updating the necessary material (the Pure and Bale Hounds, many Lodges, etc), and of course adding more new fun stuff (Lodges, Gifts, Hunting Grounds), I feel like the one topic that feels most in need of existing is an 'endgame' book. Werewolf is one of those games that has the potential to ramp up into Tier 3 and Tier 4 plots - you have apocalyptic alien super spirit monsters as the primary antagonist in the core book! - but it could use some help paving the way to such high-end threats. What happens to werewolves when they hit the upper bounds of Primal Urge is a topic I've been curious about since 1e, and with the great stuff in Equinox Road and Imperial Mysteries for Changeling and Mage, respectively, it feels like a shame to not plump those possibilities for new material.<br /> <br /> Am I crazy in wanting this? Is there anything huge I'm missing for it? Are there books that Werewolf needs more than this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:09:04-07:00","id":968221,"title":"","content":"We are getting an &quot;Elders&quot; book for Requiem, so that's another one to add to the list. Once that's out, the case for an endgame WtF book will be even stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:22:15-07:00","id":968228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like#post968202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I crazy in wanting this? Is there anything huge I'm missing for it? Are there books that Werewolf needs more than this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been talked about in many threads since second edition came out and has been something fans have wanted since peeks from open development.<br /> <br /> So far we've only been given hints of it in the various books and examples like Lycaon-Ur and the repeated term 'bodhisattva predator,' and how some feel a drive to become something more like the Firstborn or Father Wolf himself. Presumably a throwback to the werewolf's Pangaean roots, with more modern sensibilities.<br /> <br /> I won't speak for everyone but it's something much of the fandom have asked for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-12-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:38:42-07:00","id":968900,"title":"","content":"you could try to snipe ideas from the apocalypse book from werewolf the apocalypse. Might be what you're looking for. Pretty sure its under 3rd or revised edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:53:00-07:00","id":969008,"title":"","content":"I think it would relate back to finding Pangea, corrupted by the death of father wolf, and trying to address issues that might bring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:29:42-07:00","id":972307,"title":"","content":"I would love to see at least a whole chapter on Pangea and Pangeans <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:07:34-07:00","id":972329,"title":"","content":"Yes I would like to see Pangeans return as well, or at least outline some scenarios about how some could be involved in a modern game. Hosts finally reassemble to bring back their Pangean originator. A Pangean with the &quot;Time&quot; arcana threw themselves into the future. Things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:20:00-07:00","id":980810,"title":"","content":"An elders/endgame book exploring ideas for how bodhisattvas work, examining the Firstborn etc with the intent of using them as active characters with agendas that the players operate at the same level as, and some high-end global threats/goals, is all stuff I'd love to take a crack at. One could even go for grand, apocalyptic war if one wanted, with the void beyond the Warden Moon's guardian stride portrayed as a colossal invasive threat gearing up for a final showdown with Luna and her spawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:10:33-07:00","id":981368,"title":"","content":"I once played in a werewolf game... well, a game that started as a solo werewolf game, then included another werewolf (from another dimension), a mage, a shaman (that became an immortal), and me as a vampire (that was used as an experiment and had had a Helion forced in her, making her able to walk in daylight).<br /> <br /> In the climax of the first &quot;season&quot; of the game, Azlu started reforming, the player who had started the game found out he was the reincarnation of Father Wolf, we had a fistfight with Azlu before trapping her on the other side of the gauntlet, which bought us enough time to conduct a ritual that wiped out all Azlu in the world.<br /> <br /> Then, the game stopped when the GM, while he had planned other stuff, started feeling like he wouldn't be able to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:19:22-07:00","id":981394,"title":"","content":"In our current game (Changing Breeds/Werewolf), I'm steering us toward a plateau at the Feral Heart 4 or 5 level.<br /> <br /> If we get an endgame book, I'd honestly we rather get an updated Changing Breeds first, especially one that unifies the highly confusing double terminology between CB and WtF. Then we can have an endgame book that would cover all of the Pangaean Spirits' half-children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:47:16-07:00","id":981703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=981368#post981368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once played in a werewolf game... well, a game that started as a solo werewolf game, then included another werewolf (from another dimension), a mage, a shaman (that became an immortal), and me as a vampire (that was used as an experiment and had had a Helion forced in her, making her able to walk in daylight).<br /> <br /> In the climax of the first &quot;season&quot; of the game, Azlu started reforming, the player who had started the game found out he was the reincarnation of Father Wolf, we had a fistfight with Azlu before trapping her on the other side of the gauntlet, which bought us enough time to conduct a ritual that wiped out all Azlu in the world.<br /> <br /> Then, the game stopped when the GM, while he had planned other stuff, started feeling like he wouldn't be able to handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like a game so hilariously awesome that it cannot go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:38:12-07:00","id":981914,"title":"","content":"Level &quot;elder&quot; werewolf are tricky because with the long period of himbernation they are difficult to play and the example of setting that i found were of solitary one.. The one time i had a game reach that far i rule it from the following logic.<br /> <br /> The rulebook tell us that the closest thing to rank ala WtA is spiritual rank which goes<br /> <br /> Renown 0-3 = Rank 1<br /> Renown 4-7 = Rank 2<br /> Renown 8-12 = Rank 3<br /> Renown 13-18 = Rank 4<br /> Renown 19+ = Rank 5<br /> <br /> But also you have to raise your auspice renown as no other renown can be higher. So this creates a interesting contrast to WtA. In that game a elder werewolf was master of his auspice, a seasoned leader of the garou nation who guided his people in his role designated by Gaia.<br /> <br /> But there is no such leadership in WtF, the epitome of urathas is father wolf and he/she didnt need no auspice, father wolf was the apex predator doing the job of the 5 auspices by himself.<br /> <br /> Numerically it also made sense. An Werewolf could max his primary renown to be able to raise the others. For example an elodoth with honor would raise his renown to 5, that would make him a rank 2 spirit. Now he needs to get renown in other areas to get to rank 3-5. Culminating in 5 in all of them for a total of 25.<br /> <br /> With that logic in mind what i did is say that along with the himbernation and essence bleeding once reached the peak of auspice renown and Primal Urge 8 then auspice stop being important. If the elder werewolf had 5 in a out of auspice renown he could get that auspice lunar gifts.<br /> <br /> Thats how i handle it the only time it came to that as normally my players care very little about Primal urge. Also there is the Milestone gift for ideas on epic level stuff, most of them range from very useful, to marginally usefull to shitty, like the Storm Lord one from tribes of the moon. Seriously a +2 to one packmate and -2 to another? Thats a milestone gift? The Iron master is 10 times better what the hell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:28:18-07:00","id":981929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=981914#post981914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also you have to raise your auspice renown as no other renown can be higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>No longer the case in 2e; it's just pretty heavily incentivized due to greater Gift rewards and the Trait being a component of the dicepools for Hunter's Aspect and the &quot;neutral&quot; Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:57:24-07:00","id":982032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=981703#post981703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That sounds like a game so hilariously awesome that it cannot go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in addition to that, the shaman accidentally sold his soul to a demon (Inferno style, not the Descent), and when he got himself killed, me and the mage had to get the demon to release his soul so he could complete his immortalness. The demon would have played a bigger part later on. We also had to go to the realm of the dead from Geist to get one component for the ritual. Oh and the werewolf from another dimension was an amnesiac that looked just like Darius (from Wolfsbane) the first player had killed before. After dealing with Azlu, we went to the Temenos to fix something big, but we had to enter and exit through his psyche, which revealed he was actually the head or a head scientist of the SCP foundation in his home universe and that he had originally embarked on a quest to save the multiverse. Did I forget something, oh yeah, the first player (before I joined) fought and beat the Blood Hound, the servant of Thurifuge, and the last session announced the arrival of strix in town.<br /> <br /> And yes, it was all very fun. It kinda seemed like this is a GM who felt he had to exploit as many stuff he could find in the books he had as fast as possible. It made for very fast paced campaigns (visiting one of the kingdoms of the realm of the dead was like one session) where the stakes could shoot up instantly and it was pretty involving. He also liked to experiment a bit, like building a session as a series of flashbacks (with varying success, but that's experimentation for you). Thing is, sometimes, he just wouldn't know where to stop and would realize a bit late he might have bit more than he could chew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:31:32-07:00","id":982043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=981929#post981929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No longer the case in 2e; it's just pretty heavily incentivized due to greater Gift rewards and the Trait being a component of the dicepools for Hunter's Aspect and the &quot;neutral&quot; Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, though the only time i had a game to reach that level was in 1st. Still to reach rank five you need renown in all as they only get to 5 max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:15:52-07:00","id":982070,"title":"","content":"War Against the Pure. There's your End Game book. <br /> <br /> Not every game's ending revolves around reaching some kind of elder/arch-mastery/gentry level of power. Promethean's case, its becoming human. In Demon, its <i>usually</i> achieving Hell and becoming free from Compromises and the God-Machine's attention. In Mummy? Its breaking free from the cycle of servant-and-god in some way - by becoming a force of Fate, more human-like, or something else (or firmly entrenching yourself as a servant). In changeling... well, you want to avoid the &quot;end game.&quot; <br /> <br /> For Werewolf? Its re-establishing Pangaea. That involves rising up against other wolves, getting one of the Totems (or yourself) to become the new Wolf-Prime, and fixing the borders between the worlds. A more stable balance. This kind of story is really covered by the WatP book. <br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying its a subject that can't be revisited and revised, or established on a smaller scale that an individual pack can achieve, but that's the heart of the matter. We don't need a book to cover alpha wolves, because they still do the same thing as regular wolves. They dont' develop alien mindsets (at least, no more alien than anyone else with low Harmony).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:50:27-07:00","id":982082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=982032#post982032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, in addition to that, the shaman accidentally sold his soul to a demon (Inferno style, not the Descent), and when he got himself killed, me and the mage had to get the demon to release his soul so he could complete his immortalness. The demon would have played a bigger part later on. We also had to go to the realm of the dead from Geist to get one component for the ritual. Oh and the werewolf from another dimension was an amnesiac that looked just like Darius (from Wolfsbane) the first player had killed before. After dealing with Azlu, we went to the Temenos to fix something big, but we had to enter and exit through his psyche, which revealed he was actually the head or a head scientist of the SCP foundation in his home universe and that he had originally embarked on a quest to save the multiverse. Did I forget something, oh yeah, the first player (before I joined) fought and beat the Blood Hound, the servant of Thurifuge, and the last session announced the arrival of strix in town.<br /> <br /> And yes, it was all very fun. It kinda seemed like this is a GM who felt he had to exploit as many stuff he could find in the books he had as fast as possible. It made for very fast paced campaigns (visiting one of the kingdoms of the realm of the dead was like one session) where the stakes could shoot up instantly and it was pretty involving. He also liked to experiment a bit, like building a session as a series of flashbacks (with varying success, but that's experimentation for you). Thing is, sometimes, he just wouldn't know where to stop and would realize a bit late he might have bit more than he could chew.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is the most awesome thing I've ever read.<br /> <br /> Who needs horror gaming when you can have <i>this</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:11:59-07:00","id":982101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=982070#post982070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Against the Pure. There's your End Game book.<br /> <br /> Not every game's ending revolves around reaching some kind of elder/arch-mastery/gentry level of power. Promethean's case, its becoming human. In Demon, its <i>usually</i> achieving Hell and becoming free from Compromises and the God-Machine's attention. In Mummy? Its breaking free from the cycle of servant-and-god in some way - by becoming a force of Fate, more human-like, or something else (or firmly entrenching yourself as a servant). In changeling... well, you want to avoid the &quot;end game.&quot;<br /> <br /> For Werewolf? Its re-establishing Pangaea. That involves rising up against other wolves, getting one of the Totems (or yourself) to become the new Wolf-Prime, and fixing the borders between the worlds. A more stable balance. This kind of story is really covered by the WatP book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't. War Against the Pure is specifically about war, whether it's just simple organized brutality, or the Silver Crusade, a massive sacred hunt. It has very, very little to do with personal development. And while 'not every game's ending revolves around reaching some elder/arch-mastery/gentry level of power', werewolf's clearly does, as we see from Lycaon-Ur, Dorj Tserendjav, the Storm Lord Abni-Gur, and even Urazakh-Angir back in first edition. What they did, what they are, isn't even remotely covered in War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are shapeshifters and half spirit. Everything about them screams 'becoming something else.' And considering the way Werewolf, and second edition in general, has broken away from traditional World of Darkness growth, there's no reason that 'something else' should just be 'a werewolf with bigger dicepools.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:35:45-07:00","id":982430,"title":"","content":"Uh, maybe things changed since 1ed, but isn't re-establishing Pangea the goal of the Pure ? I feel Forsaken are really fighting for a status quo. From what I remember understanding, Pangea didn't really have much of a border and Father Wolf was super busy keeping things in order. His death is what created the gauntlet which is more difficult for spirits (and humans) to pass through to mess things up on the other side. If anything, Pangea ending made the two worlds easier to keep separate. That's why the Pure's goal is problematic (especially the Predator Kings who are the only ones who are truly interested by what Pangea represents) because besides being a genocide on all non-pure, it means sending the world back into a more chaotic state.<br /> <br /> So if there is a usual endgame scenario for Werewolf, it really wouldn't be about bringing Pangea back, unless you're playing the Pure. But again, maybe things have changed in 2ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=982082#post982082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is the most awesome thing I've ever read.<br /> <br /> Who needs horror gaming when you can have <i>this</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>His games were a lot of fun and really awesome. That said, sometimes, the overload of stuff could be a bit too much (it got too much for him in the end), and while his plots are great, he's not the best GM in terms of roleplay (his is a little wooden) and coming up with really memorable and unique characters, although he did get better, but the pressure he could put on the players was sometimes enough to counterbalance that. That said, even being one of the better games I've played (and him being one of the best GMs I've had), it wasn't THE best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:45:43-07:00","id":982437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=982430#post982430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, maybe things changed since 1ed, but isn't re-establishing Pangea the goal of the Pure ? I feel Forsaken are really fighting for a status quo. From what I remember understanding, Pangea didn't really have much of a border and Father Wolf was super busy keeping things in order. His death is what created the gauntlet which is more difficult for spirits (and humans) to pass through to mess things up on the other side. If anything, Pangea ending made the two worlds easier to keep separate. That's why the Pure's goal is problematic (especially the Predator Kings who are the only ones who are truly interested by what Pangea represents) because besides being a genocide on all non-pure, it means sending the world back into a more chaotic state.<br /> <br /> So if there is a usual endgame scenario for Werewolf, it really wouldn't be about bringing Pangea back, unless you're playing the Pure. But again, maybe things have changed in 2ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't become the goal of the Forsaken, as far as I know. But as the game has moved more definitively in the realm of, 'you are not human,' and you aren't the spirit or human police, it's a much more reasonable goal for a Forsaken, or group of them, to have, though it would likely be considered extremist.<br /> <br /> What has come up is the potential resurrection of Father Wolf. It seemed like an entirely impossible thing to happen in first edition. Dark Eras has explained how Pangaeans work and made it clearly a possibility, even if it's a far-fetched one. Since Father Wolf is Pangaea, at least according to some theories, his resurrection might bring it back. There's more than enough cues to work off of that in the books, though I don't think it's put forward as a direct goal, parallels are brought up, for instance Dorj Tserendjav and Fenris-Ur's attempts to unearth long lost Firstborn, and the former's resurrection of one.<br /> <br /> I've loved the game since it came out and second edition really fixed what made it a heartbreaker for me. I trust the developer and writing team, if we get anything in terms of an endgame book it will be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-05-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:25:15-07:00","id":992501,"title":"","content":"Something I was thinking about, since werewolves are canonically actually (part?) pangeans and pangeans have access to supernal magic, shouldn't elder/endgame (high PU) werewolves get limited access as well? Not sure how it would work as there is probably not enough space in an such a book for the full magic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:47:51-07:00","id":992552,"title":"","content":"That's basically covered by the freeform nature of Influences and the power of Gifts being pretty solid all around. One thing you don't do is go the route of giving one splat the powers of another. I mean, Mage has its issues I don't agree with so I'd really rather not see them pulled into Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The simple way I go about it is to reintroduce Milestone Gifts with a modified way Interlocks and Ciphers work in Demon. You have all 5 Facets cut into you and its expressed through Renown in a way that's uniquely Werewolf is what we currently have. The Milestone Gift would be a capstone requiring all 5 and showing how your bond with a particular resonance reshapes you or the world around you. In game I'd probably say you undertake a quest involving a Rank 6+ spirit to gain the power, but all in all it seems like an elegant way to make something powerful, but uniquely tied to the story the player is trying to tell about your character.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's specifically for Shadow Gifts. Moon Milestone Gifts likely go with empowering your Auspice Abilities spectacularly. Although I'm the sort that'd require you to learn all 3 Moon Gift Sets for your Auspice and have a Greater Lune pop down and get all up in your business about it.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts could probably go the same route as Shadow Gifts, but likely much more toned down since you're basically doing a form of meditation to find the power within yourself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:09:12-07:00","id":993389,"title":"","content":"To me different forms of immortality is a must, from an essential spirit to living on forever in the songs and stories of the People. That's a glorious goal after a long campaign, I would think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:24:20-07:00","id":993564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=992552#post992552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's basically covered by the freeform nature of Influences and the power of Gifts being pretty solid all around. One thing you don't do is go the route of giving one splat the powers of another. I mean, Mage has its issues I don't agree with so I'd really rather not see them pulled into Werewolf.<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, yes in that influences and the right gifts are freeform enough to be able to do similar stuff, no in the sens that it still isn't supernal magic. Of course this only maters in a cross over where &quot;The Sundered World&quot; is taken as canon but (at least from an academic viewpoint) I find this really interesting and think an end game book should at least mention it (even if it is just a sidebar with some suggestions!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [...]<br /> The simple way I go about it is to reintroduce Milestone Gifts with a modified way Interlocks and Ciphers work in Demon. You have all 5 Facets cut into you and its expressed through Renown in a way that's uniquely Werewolf is what we currently have. The Milestone Gift would be a capstone requiring all 5 and showing how your bond with a particular resonance reshapes you or the world around you. In game I'd probably say you undertake a quest involving a Rank 6+ spirit to gain the power, but all in all it seems like an elegant way to make something powerful, but uniquely tied to the story the player is trying to tell about your character.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's specifically for Shadow Gifts. Moon Milestone Gifts likely go with empowering your Auspice Abilities spectacularly. Although I'm the sort that'd require you to learn all 3 Moon Gift Sets for your Auspice and have a Greater Lune pop down and get all up in your business about it.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts could probably go the same route as Shadow Gifts, but likely much more toned down since you're basically doing a form of meditation to find the power within yourself.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like great ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:20:13-07:00","id":993699,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the reason Pangaeans have Arcana isn't because they actually have Supernal magic, but just because it's the easiest way to quickly reflect how much greater their powers are than normal spirits, and because it's in a crossover chapter. I'm not sure they'd have Arcana if they weren't presented in a combined Mage/Werewolf setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:17:34-07:00","id":993729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=993699#post993699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the reason Pangaeans have Arcana isn't because they actually have Supernal magic, but just because it's the easiest way to quickly reflect how much greater their powers are than normal spirits, and because it's in a crossover chapter. I'm not sure they'd have Arcana if they weren't presented in a combined Mage/Werewolf setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, from a more Watsonian perspective, there's that whole &quot;pillars of the world&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:28:52-07:00","id":993736,"title":"","content":"Free Council would not like hearing that. I don't think any Awakened would like hearing that.<br /> <br /> At least, after someone described to them what Pangaeans were and if you managed to get them to believe in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:16:49-07:00","id":993792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=993736#post993736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Council would not like hearing that. I don't think any Awakened would like hearing that.<br /> <br /> At least, after someone described to them what Pangaeans were and if you managed to get them to believe in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're going with &quot;pillars of the world&quot; the Mages could probably explain it the way they explain Sekhem sorcery as manipulating reality &quot;barehanded&quot; (I'm paraphrasing here from the Mummy/Mage crossover stuff) where Supernal magic manipulates it indirectly through Platonic symbols.<br /> <br /> Which would at least be interesting to Mages before it becomes infuriating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T18:09:44-07:00","id":993814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=993736#post993736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Council would not like hearing that. I don't think any Awakened would like hearing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd probably change their minds once they realize they can abuse Pangaean hearts to create demenses greater than that of any created through soulstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Well, I think the reason Pangaeans have Arcana isn't because they actually have Supernal magic, but just because it's the easiest way to quickly reflect how much greater their powers are than normal spirits, and because it's in a crossover chapter. I'm not sure they'd have Arcana if they weren't presented in a combined Mage/Werewolf setting.</span> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I don't agree with this considering how omphalos stones function. Seems its much more than just abstraction.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:32:23-07:00","id":993841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=993814#post993814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd probably change their minds once they realize they can abuse Pangaean hearts to create demenses greater than that of any created through soulstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be hard to figure out, since they've been effectively ejected from the universe and no longer exist except in the form of remnants that offer no such special advantage. You could sell t-shirts at the Convocation, though. 'Our Ancestors Knew Of The Pillars Of The World, And All I Got Was A Demesne.'<br /> <br /> On to more pertinent matters, while I appreciate some people may like the idea of gaining Awakening-level control over their Influence, I don't think it really fits werewolf very well even at a bodhisattva level. The only great advantage in being able to Pattern, Unravel or Make the Hunt would be to not have to use the Sacred Hunt rite, but at that point you're just switching it out for something else. You could tag other Influences to it depending on how you lean but something more like Vampire's Blood Sorcery, except with 'spirit magic' would make more sense.<br /> <br /> I think a major difference in the book would be its focus on the pack, rather than the lone wolf. While I do believe a lone werewolf should be represented in such an endgame book, for playing the game you would want to focus on a pack. And in this you have a different approach than you do with vampires and mages, who make those last steps alone and occasionally over the corpses of former coteries and cabals. A werewolf with Primal Urge 10 is devastating with the rules given. How much moreso a pack of werewolves at 8-10, with a suitably powerful totem that likely swells with such power it will have to start stepping away from the world, or risk destroying it. What are the Wolf-blooded of this pack? What are the humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:41:21-07:00","id":993843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/968202-what-would-an-endgame-book-look-like?p=993841#post993841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be hard to figure out</div> </div> </div> </div>The opening fiction of Sundered World has a modern mage who is aware of what Omphalos Stones are (though they are effectively myth before the events of the fiction show proof for the myth).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are the Wolf-blooded of this pack? What are the humans? </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting idea...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-26-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}